{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh removed his signet ring.</b> The giving of the king's signet ring is a sign for the one to whom he gives it, that he is to be second to him in greatness." "<b>Garments of fine linen.</b> It is a precious thing in Egypt." "<b>A chain.</b> A necklace. And because it is set with rings it is called רְבִיד. So too ״מַרְבַדִּים רָבַדְתִּי עַרְשִׂי״ (Proverbs 7) — I paved my bed with pavings, in Mishnaic language: מֻקָּף רוֹבְדִין שֶׁל אֶבֶן, upon the רֹבֶד in the Temple court — and that is a pavement."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:02.360899859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}